<title>BRAZIL: Brazil cuts export tax on sugar, alcohol - Cenbank.</title>
<headline>Brazil cuts export tax on sugar, alcohol - Cenbank.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil has cut to zero a tax on the export of a range of sugar and alcohol products, the Central Bank said Friday.</p>
<p>The measure came into effect Friday when the bank published a decree detailing the changes.  </p>
<p>The decree listed several types of sugar products, including refined sugar, which would be taxed at zero percent, down from a previous 40 percent rate.  </p>
<p>The decree also said export tariffs on alcohol products had been cut to zero percent.</p>
<p>(( -- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 3141193))</p>
